# Korkut settings. ./install.sh creates .env with the two secrets below; everything else here is
# optional. To change a setting, add the line to .env and run ./install.sh again. The real .env
# is gitignored; never put secrets in this committed example.

# ================= Model gateway (written by ./install.sh) =================
# LLMR_MASTER_KEY=               # seals the AI provider keys; keep a copy, never change it
# LLMR_TOKEN=                    # what Korkut presents to the gateway

# ================= Address =================
# KORKUT_HTTP_PORT=8090          # http://localhost:8090
# KORKUT_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1  # this machine only; 0.0.0.0 opens Korkut to your network
# KORKUT_APP_URL=http://localhost:8090   # the address links in e-mails point at

# ================= AI models =================
# Providers, keys and models are chosen in the app: Ayarlar → Yapay zeka (office owner). Keys are
# kept sealed in the model gateway, never in this file. Optional limits on Korkut's own use:
# KORKUT_OFFICE_TOKEN_BUDGET=0   # monthly prompt + completion tokens; 0 = unlimited
# KORKUT_MAX_TOKENS=8192         # largest reply asked of the chat model

# ================= Sign-in with Google (optional) =================
# Without these, members sign in with e-mail and password. To add Google, create a "Web
# application" OAuth client in the Google Cloud Console and register the redirect URI on it.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8090/api/auth/google/callback

# ================= Outbound e-mail (optional) =================
# Invitations and password resets are e-mailed from one SMTP account; unset, they are only
# logged. For Gmail use an App Password, not your login password.
# KORKUT_SMTP_USER=
# KORKUT_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# KORKUT_SMTP_FROM=
# KORKUT_SMTP_FROM_NAME=Korkut
# KORKUT_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# KORKUT_SMTP_PORT=587

# ================= Telegram (optional) =================
# The office bot is set up in the app: Ayarlar → Telegram (office owner). Korkut polls Telegram, so
# no public address is needed. Only to use your own Bot API server:
# KORKUT_TELEGRAM_API_URL=https://api.telegram.org

# ================= Secrets =================
# Generated on first start into the `secrets` volume and reused; set them here only to manage
# them yourself. Changing KORKUT_SECRET signs everyone out; losing KORKUT_TOTP_KEY voids 2FA setups.
# KORKUT_SECRET=                 # 32+ bytes, e.g. openssl rand -hex 32
# KORKUT_TOTP_KEY=               # base64 of 32 bytes, e.g. openssl rand -base64 32
# The database is only reachable inside the compose network, so local defaults are used. Set
# these before the FIRST start to choose your own; changing them later needs a new database.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# KORKUT_APP_DB_PASSWORD=

# ================= Documents =================
# Uploaded documents live on the `objects` volume. To keep them in an S3-compatible server:
# KORKUT_STORAGE=s3
# KORKUT_MINIO_ENDPOINT=host:9000
# KORKUT_MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=
# KORKUT_MINIO_SECRET_KEY=
# KORKUT_MINIO_SECURE=1          # https
# Scanned PDFs are read by the bundled OCR service; this tunes its languages:
# KORKUT_OCR_LANGS=tur+eng

# ================= Behind a reverse proxy =================
# KORKUT_SECURE_COOKIES=1        # when served over HTTPS
# Name the header your proxy sets to the real client IP so rate limits see each client
# (Caddy/nginx: X-Real-IP). Leave unset when nothing in front overwrites it.
# KORKUT_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=X-Real-IP

# ================= Monitoring (optional) =================
# `docker compose --profile ops up -d` starts Grafana on :3000; then send telemetry to it:
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://lgtm:4317
